-- title:
--   The small pro-étale site of a scheme: its topology as a restricted topology, its Zariski topology, and basic instances
-- statement:
--   For a scheme $X$, the small pro-étale site $X_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}}$ has as objects the schemes $U$ with a weakly étale morphism $U \to X$ (Mathlib's definition, following Bhatt–Scholze, Definition 4.1.1); its topology is generated by the precoverage pulled back from the big pro-étale precoverage (fpqc-type covers by weakly étale morphisms) along the forgetful functor to schemes.
--
--   Contents of this file:
--   1. The pro-étale topology on $X_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}}$ coincides with the topology restricted from the big pro-étale topology on schemes over $X$ along the forgetful functor $X_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}} \to \mathrm{Sch}/X$.
--   2. Definition of the **Zariski topology** on $X_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}}$: the topology induced on weakly étale $X$-schemes by covering families of open immersions.
--   3. The pro-étale precoverage on $X_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}}$ contains isomorphisms and is stable under composition and base change.
--   4. Every morphism $U \to V$ in $X_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}}$ is weakly étale as a morphism of schemes (since $U \to X$ and $V \to X$ are).
--
--   **Formalization Note** `X : Scheme.{u}`; the site is `X.ProEt = MorphismProperty.Over @WeaklyEtale ⊤ X` from Mathlib, with topology `ProEt.topology X` and precoverage `ProEt.precoverage X`. The declarations are `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.topology_eq_restrictedTopology`, `ProEt.zariskiTopology` (defined as `smallGrothendieckTopology (Q := @WeaklyEtale) @IsOpenImmersion X`) and anonymous instances for `HasIsos`, `IsStableUnderComposition`, `IsStableUnderBaseChange` and `WeaklyEtale f.left`.
-- source:
--   B. Bhatt, P. Scholze, The pro-étale topology for schemes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198 (v2, 17 Dec 2014). Lean source: idealson-nexources/proetale (fork of chrisflav/proetale by C. Merten, J. Jiang and contributors, Apache-2.0), commit 2983805, file Proetale/Topology/Proetale/Basic.lean (declarations needed by the transplanted proofs, unused ones removed).

